<zk xmlns:n="native">
    <n:h1>WCAG 2.1 - 4.1.3 status messages</n:h1>
    <label multiline="true">
        1. open devtools and find #za11y-announcer, then its [role=log][aria-live=polite] region.
           On page load it must be EMPTY - arriving on a page is not a status message
        2. in the first paging (detailed), press the "next" arrow - the polite region receives
           "Currently displaying items 11-20 out of 100", matching the [ 11 - 20 / 100 ] shown beside it
        3. press "next" again - a second message arrives for the next range
        4. in the second paging (not detailed), press "next" - NOTHING is announced:
           no summary is shown there, so there is no status message to speak
        5. press "rerender" - watch the first paging's node get replaced in devtools to
           confirm it really was rebuilt. It stays on the same page, so no new message
           arrives.
        6. press "empty" - the summary disappears from the screen along with every item,
           so nothing is announced.
        7. with a screen reader on, only steps 2 and 3 should be spoken, and each AFTER the
           refocused arrow is read out - the announcement must not interrupt focus
    </label>
    <vlayout spacing="10px" hflex="1">
        <paging id="detailed" totalSize="100" pageSize="10" detailed="true"/>
        <paging id="plain" totalSize="100" pageSize="10"/>
        <hlayout>
            <button id="rerender" label="rerender"
                onClick='detailed.setPageIncrement(detailed.getPageIncrement() == 10 ? 8 : 10)'/>
            <button id="empty" label="empty" onClick='detailed.setTotalSize(0)'/>
        </hlayout>
    </vlayout>
</zk>
